fensively (e.g., defending f7 or moving the queen).\n- It cannot be immediately challenged by pawns.\n- It improves piece activity at a critical moment.\n\nReason:  \nNf3-e5 is the most aggressive and positionally sound move, seizing the initiative and increasing pressure on Black’s camp. It maximizes activity and follows opening principles of rapid development and central control.\n\nAnswer: N: f3-e5"}
