4 now would be met by ...Nxd4 due to no support yet, losing the pawn unless recaptured — and after Nxd4, Qxd4?? Qxd4, Bxd4, White loses material.\n\nB: f1-c4 avoids premature pawn grabs, develops actively, and keeps options open.\n\nReason: Developing the bishop to c4 exerts immediate pressure on the center and f7, supports future central control, and avoids tactical pitfalls from capturing in the center prematurely. It's a principled opening move (similar to the Italian Game idea), promoting rapid development and initiative.\n\nAnswer: B: f1-c4"}
